<p>"How much is this going to cost?" It's the first thing people ask when they press a thumb into the fascia board and it gives. That's fair. Nobody wants to open up a roof edge without knowing what they're in for.</p>

<p>Here's the straight answer for Huntsville and North Alabama, what moves the number up or down, and the part most pricing guides leave out: the gutters hanging on that board.</p>

<h2>What Fascia Repair Costs in North Alabama</h2>

<p>Fascia repair typically costs <strong>$5-15 per linear foot</strong> in Huntsville and across North Alabama, depending on how far the damage goes, the material you choose, and how hard the roof edge is to reach. Most homes need <strong>10-40 feet</strong> replaced. That's usually isolated sections where a gutter leaked or overflowed for years, not the whole house.</p>

<p>Put those together and the wood work on a typical job lands somewhere around <strong>$50-600</strong>.</p>

